{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-57735","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66370","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-57736","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66371","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-66372","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-66373","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-66374","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-66375","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-66376","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-57737","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66377","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57738","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66378","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-57739","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66379","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-66380","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-66381","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-57740","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66382","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-66383","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-57741","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66384","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-66385","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-66386","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-57742","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-57743","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66387","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57744","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66388","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-57745","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-57746","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66389","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57747","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66390","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-57748","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66391","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-57749","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66392","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-57750","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66393","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-66394","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-66395","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-57751","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57754","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66396","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-57753","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66397","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-57755","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66398","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-57757","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66399","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-57759","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57761","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66400","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-57762","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57764","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66401","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-66402","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-66403","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-57763","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57766","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66404","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-66405","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-57765","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57768","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66406","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-57767","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57770","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66407","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-57769","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57772","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66408","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-57771","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57774","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66409","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-57773","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66410","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57776","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66411","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-57777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66412","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-66413","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-66414","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-57778","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-57779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66415","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57780","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66416","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-57781","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66417","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-57782","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66418","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-66419","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-66420","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-66421","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-66422","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57783","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66423","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-66424","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-66425","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66426","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-66427","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66428","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-66429","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-57784","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66430","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-57786","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57789","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66431","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-66432","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-66433","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-57788","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57791","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66434","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-66435","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-66436","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-57790","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57793","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66437","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-66438","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-66439","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-66440","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-57792","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66441","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-66442","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-66443","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-66444","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-66445","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57795","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57797","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66446","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-57796","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57799","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66447","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-57798","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57801","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66448","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-57800","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66449","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-66450","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-66451","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-66452","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-66453","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57803","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66454","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-66455","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-57804","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57807","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66456","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-66457","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-57806","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66458","text":"4. "},{"id":"spn-66459","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-66460","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]},{"id":"blk-57809","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66461","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-57810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66462","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-57811","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66463","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-66464","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-66465","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-66466","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-66467","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57812","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66468","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-66469","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-66470","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-66471","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-57813","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66472","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-66473","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-66474","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-57815","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66475","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-66476","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-66477","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-66478","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-57817","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66479","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-66480","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-66481","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-66482","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-57819","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66483","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-66484","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-57821","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66485","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-66486","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-57823","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57826","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66487","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-66488","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-57825","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57828","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66489","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-66490","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-57827","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57830","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66491","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-66492","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-57829","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66493","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-66494","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-57831","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66495","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-66496","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-66497","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-57833","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57836","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66498","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-66499","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-66500","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-57835","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66501","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-66502","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-66503","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-57837","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66504","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-66505","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]},{"id":"blk-57840","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66506","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-66507","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-57841","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66508","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-66509","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-57843","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57846","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66510","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-66511","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-57845","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66512","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-57847","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57849","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66513","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-66514","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-66515","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agentelic or the user's own API key) processes. SpecPrompt is a tool, not an agent. The MCP server version ("},{"id":"spn-66516","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_compile"},{"id":"spn-66517","text":") returns the prompt for the agent t